<item>
            <title>[LU-20832] llite: GETINFO_V2 returns a wrong rdev for device files</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20832</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;LL_IOC_MDC_GETINFO_V2&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;IOC_MDC_GETFILEINFO_V2&lt;/tt&gt; return a wrong device number for a character or block device.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The client sends the device number in the old 16-bit encoding (&lt;tt&gt;old_encode_dev()&lt;/tt&gt; in &lt;tt&gt;ll_mknod()&lt;/tt&gt;), and the MDT returns it the same way in &lt;tt&gt;mbo_rdev&lt;/tt&gt;. &lt;tt&gt;ll_update_inode()&lt;/tt&gt; decodes it with &lt;tt&gt;old_decode_dev()&lt;/tt&gt;, so &lt;tt&gt;stat(2)&lt;/tt&gt; is right. The V2 arm in &lt;tt&gt;ll_dir_ioctl()&lt;/tt&gt; calls &lt;tt&gt;MAJOR()&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;MINOR()&lt;/tt&gt; on the raw value:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;stx.stx_rdev_major = MAJOR(body-&amp;gt;mbo_rdev);
stx.stx_rdev_minor = MINOR(body-&amp;gt;mbo_rdev);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So every device node has major 0 and a wrong minor.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Measured on 2.17.57, ldiskfs, 2 MDTs. Stock &lt;tt&gt;lustre.ko&lt;/tt&gt; and fixed &lt;tt&gt;lustre.ko&lt;/tt&gt; run one after the other, twice each:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;mknod          stat(2)   V1 (raw st_rdev)  V2 stock   V2 fixed
c 10 200       10:200    10:200            0:2760     10:200
b 8 1          8:1       8:1               0:2049     8:1
c 300 5        44:5      44:5              0:11269    44:5
c 4 1048000    253:192   253:192           0:64960    253:192
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The V1 arm is correct: it copies the raw value into &lt;tt&gt;st_rdev&lt;/tt&gt;, and userspace &lt;tt&gt;major()&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;minor()&lt;/tt&gt; read the same bits. (c 300 5 shows as 44:5 everywhere, because the old encoding has 8 bits each. That is a separate limit, not this bug.)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Who sees it: llapi callers of the V2 ioctls, for example a find that reads &lt;tt&gt;stx_rdev_major&lt;/tt&gt;/&lt;tt&gt;stx_rdev_minor&lt;/tt&gt;. No tool in master prints this field today.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: decode with &lt;tt&gt;old_decode_dev()&lt;/tt&gt; first, as &lt;tt&gt;ll_update_inode()&lt;/tt&gt; does.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
